POE2TRADE.DB SUBMODULE — UPDATED 2025-09-07

Overview
The `poe2trade.db` package contains the offline data pipeline and model
artifacts used by the app GUI overlays. It owns category data under `db/files/`,
generates feature matrices, and trains both supervised regressors and
unsupervised KNN models.

Top‑Level Actions (python -m poe2trade.db)
- scrape_selenium: Drive the PoE2 trade site with Selenium and save JSON dumps.
- parse: Flatten the per-item JSON into tidy tables (xlsx/parquet).
- matrix: Build feature matrices (overlay + model variants).
- train_super: Train supervised regressors (XGB/RF/GBR) per category/segment.
- score_super: Score matrices with trained models and update bucket stats.
- train_unsuper: Train KNN reference models per category/segment.

Examples
- python -m poe2trade.db scrape_selenium Body_Armour Boots
- python -m poe2trade.db parse Body_Armour
- python -m poe2trade.db matrix Body_Armour
- python -m poe2trade.db train_super Body_Armour
- python -m poe2trade.db score_super Body_Armour
- python -m poe2trade.db train_unsuper Body_Armour

Key Scripts (how they connect)
- __main__.py: CLI that dispatches to the actions listed above.
- scrape_selenium_cat.py: Reads `db/files/category_items.xlsx`, opens the site
  with Selenium, applies filters, and writes one JSON file per item under
  `db/files/<Category_With_Underscores>/`.
- parse_cat.py: Uses `utils/parse_utils.py` to flatten those JSON files into a
  single `<category>_agg_parsed.xlsx` and `.parquet` in the same folder.
- matrix_cat.py: Uses `utils/matrix_utils.py:build_feature_matrix` to create:
  - `<category>_feature_matrix_overlay.(xlsx|parquet)`
  - `<category>_feature_matrix_model.(xlsx|parquet)`
  The model variant is pruned for model training; both standardize columns
  to lowercase and compute normalized defences `ar_norm/ev_norm/es_norm`.
- train_super_cat.py: Calls `utils/train_utils.py:train_super_model_from_matrix`
  to fit XGB/RF/GBR (depending on project flags). Saves pickles under
  `db/super_models/` with per‑model READMEs. Models are per armour segment
  (e.g. `body_armour_ar_ev_only_xgb_model.pkl`); jewellery has no segment key.
- score_super_cat.py: Calls `utils/score_super_utils.py:score_matrix` to score
  matrices, produce per‑segment spreadsheets and histograms, and update
  `db/super_models/category_segment_stats.json` (used at runtime for
  bucket labelling and confidence intervals).
- train_unsuper_cat.py: Calls `utils/train_utils.py:train_unsuper_model_from_matrix`
  to build KNN reference models per category/segment. Saves pickles under
  `db/unsuper_models/` containing `nn_model`, `feature_cols`, `scaler_data`,
  `overlay_df` (for GUI overlay rows), and `row_indices`.

Important Folders
- db/files/
  - category_items.xlsx: Source list of items per category for scraping.
  - <Category>/
    - Raw JSON dumps per item.
    - <category>_agg_parsed.(xlsx|parquet)
    - <category>_feature_matrix_overlay.(xlsx|parquet)
    - <category>_feature_matrix_model.(xlsx|parquet)
- db/base_icons/
  - PNG icons by base type (used by the unsupervised “Price Mirror” overlay).
  - Built by `utils/get_icon_utils.py` alongside `db/files/base_images.json`.
- db/super_models/
  - <base>_<model>_model.pkl (e.g. `body_armour_ar_ev_only_xgb_model.pkl`)
  - <base>_<model>_model_readme.txt
  - category_segment_stats.json (bucket intervals + summary stats)
- db/unsuper_models/
  - <base>_knn_model.pkl (or `<base>_<segment>_knn_model.pkl` for armour)
  - <base>_knn_model_readme.txt

Naming Conventions
- “Category” filenames use underscores: `Body Armour` -> `Body_Armour`.
- Armour is segmented by defence combos: `ar_only`, `ev_only`, `es_only`,
  `ar_ev_only`, `ar_es_only`, `ev_es_only`, `all_three`.
- Supervised model base name: `<category>` for jewellery or
  `<category>_<segment>` for armour.

How the App Uses These Artifacts
- Supervised overlay (Ctrl+1 in the GUI):
  - `utils/ml_super_utils.call_ml` loads any available regressors under
    `db/super_models/`, predicts, aggregates, and bucketises using
    `category_segment_stats.json`. Charts are rendered via `utils/chart_utils.py`.
- Unsupervised overlay (Ctrl+2 “Price Mirror”):
  - `utils/ml_unsuper_utils.call_ml` loads the appropriate KNN bundle under
    `db/unsuper_models/`, filters by a runtime price threshold, and returns
    an `overlay_df` slice for side‑by‑side comparison. Icons are resolved via
    `db/files/base_images.json` and `db/base_icons/`.

Dependencies
- Core: pandas, numpy, scikit‑learn, xgboost, matplotlib, openpyxl.
- Scraping (selenium action): selenium, pyautogui, Chrome.
- Optional: shap (feature explanations for supervised models).
